# Reset a trap, let it kill a hostile twice, and photograph Semirath's favour
# between every step. Read by tools/check_favour_awards.sh, bd inc-rgzr.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/kobold-rogue-seed1.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/favour-trap.keys 1
#
# Trap::TriggerTrap (src/Feature.cpp) pays the character who RESET the trap
# when it springs on a creature hostile to him: CR * 50 favour to Semirath if
# the trap kills it, and another CR * 50 the first time that trap pays at all.
# So one trap, two kills: the first kill pays both awards, the second only the
# kill award, because the first left XP_GAINED on the trap. The same branch
# pays experience too -- 100 + 25 * CR, once per trap -- through GainXP, which
# never had this defect, so the sidebar's XP shows on its own that the
# once-per-trap branch ran on the first kill and not on the second.
#
# The Handle Device checks on the way pay favour as well, because Semirath's
# FAVOURED_SKILLS list holds Handle Device. Their lines are photographed so the
# check can compute that award, and the sheets bracket them separately.
#
# THE STEPS, and why each one is there:
#
#   Freeze Monsters      on for the whole session. The manes never walks, so
#                        no monster-AI choice decides whether it reaches the
#                        trap.
#   Become Divine        Semirath the patron. His EV_CALC_FAVOUR scales by
#     Champion           ranks in Perform and Bluff; this fixture has none.
#   Create Trap          a deathblade scythe one square east. It is level 8:
#                        6d4+24 slashing kills a manes outright, and its save
#                        is DC 23 against a manes' +2 Reflex.
#   @until "A trap!" s   a created trap is hidden; search until it is found.
#                        DisarmTrap refuses a trap that is not found.
#   u Handle Device y    disarm it -- a reset needs a disarmed trap.
#   u Handle Device r y  reset it, standing beside it. RESET_BY is what the
#                        awards read.
#   Learn Any Spell      Force Bolt. Its knockback (AD_KNOC, EV_PUSH) moves
#                        the target through Creature::Walk, which fires traps.
#   LEFT                 the trap is now two squares east.
#   Monster Summoning    a manes one square east, between the kobold and the
#                        trap. A summoned creature on the trap square does
#                        not fire it, so the manes is placed beside it. A
#                        manes is mindless and evil, so it is hostile without
#                        being struck (TargetSystem::RacialHostility).
#   m Force Bolt RIGHT   the bolt pushes the manes 1d4 squares east. The trap
#                        is the first square it enters, so the distance does
#                        not matter. The game prints "Your force bolt kills a
#                        manes" for the death, because the pusher gets the
#                        credit; the trap's own Reflex save line (DC 23) is
#                        what shows the trap sprang.
#   s                    one turn, so the sidebar redraws its XP total. The
#                        manes is frozen, so the turn changes nothing else.
#   RIGHT, reset         the second kill: step back beside the trap and reset
#                        it, then repeat the summon and the bolt.
#
# THE ROLLS are forced by tools/check_favour_awards.sh, not left to the seed:
# INCURSION_FORCE_SAVE_ROLL=1 (the manes fails its Reflex save),
# INCURSION_LOF_FORCE_ROLL=20 (the bolt hits), INCURSION_RUNTO_SKILL_ROLL=20
# (the search and every Handle Device check succeed).

w
@while "Enter wizard mode" y
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC

w
@choose "Become Divine Champion"
"Semirath"
ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE

d
DOWN*20
@dump:favour-champion
ESC

w
@choose "Create Trap"
"deathblade scythe trap"
ENTER
RIGHT
ENTER
@until "A trap!" s

u
@choose "Handle Device"
@expect "Disarm -- Handle Device"
y
@dump:disarm

u
@choose "Handle Device"
@while "Reset trap or salvage" r
@expect "Reset -- Handle Device"
y
@dump:reset

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Force Bolt" ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC

# --- the first kill: the kill award and the once-per-trap award -----------
LEFT
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Demons"
@choose "manes"
RIGHT
ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
s
@dump:armed

d
DOWN*20
@dump:favour-armed
ESC

m
@cursorto:mark "Force Bolt" DOWN
ENTER
RIGHT ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
s
@dump:kill1
@while "more --" SPACE

d
DOWN*20
@dump:favour-kill1
ESC

# --- the second kill, on the same trap: the kill award alone ----------------
RIGHT
u
@choose "Handle Device"
@while "Reset trap or salvage" r
@expect "Reset -- Handle Device"
y
@dump:reset2

LEFT
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Demons"
@choose "manes"
RIGHT
ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
s
@dump:armed2

d
DOWN*20
@dump:favour-armed2
ESC

m
@cursorto:mark "Force Bolt" DOWN
ENTER
RIGHT ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
s
@dump:kill2
@while "more --" SPACE

d
DOWN*20
@dump:favour-kill2
ESC

v
@dump:messages
@while "Messages" ESC
